WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Better reflection starts with better questions.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.455
What happened?

00:00:03.455 --> 00:00:04.640
What was I trying to accomplish?

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.600
What did I expect?

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.415
What surprised me?

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:07.600
What evidence do I have?

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.760
These questions slow the move from emotional reaction to conclusion.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.520
They help separate the event itself from the first story the mind creates about the event.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.410
Assumption questions are especially useful.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.450
What did I assume about the task, the user, the system, the timeline, the team,

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.240
or my own skill?

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.080
Which assumptions were supported by evidence, and which were guesses?

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.230
Many failures are not caused by lack of effort.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.740
They are caused by reasonable-looking assumptions that were never tested soon enough.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.175
Outcome questions connect reflection to improvement.

00:00:32.175 --> 00:00:33.015
What worked?

00:00:33.015 --> 00:00:33.845
What failed?

00:00:33.845 --> 00:00:34.675
What was lucky?

00:00:34.675 --> 00:00:35.515
What was repeatable?

00:00:35.515 --> 00:00:36.680
What would I do differently next time?

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.840
What should become a checklist, pattern, default, or warning sign?

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.970
These questions turn reflection into a practical diagnosis rather than a general feeling

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.392
that something was good or bad.

00:00:45.392 --> 00:00:47.510
Blame questions usually produce weaker learning.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.365
Who is at fault?

00:00:48.365 --> 00:00:49.470
Why did I mess this up?

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:50.710
Why did they not know better?

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.755
These questions narrow attention and often make people defensive.

00:00:53.755 --> 00:00:56.840
Useful reflective questions stay specific and action-oriented.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.520
They ask what the situation teaches, what can be improved,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.600
and how the next attempt can be better supported.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.020
The tone matters because people are more likely to learn when the question gives them room

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.160
to be accurate instead of merely protective.
